  "note": "Figma no longer publishes one master 'all shortcuts' Help Center page (it moved the full list into an in-app panel opened with Ctrl+Shift+? / Cmd+Shift+?); this file is compiled from the current set of per-topic official Help Center articles listed in `sources`, one per Figma Design section (Tools, Zoom & view, Editing objects, Text, Boolean groups, Components, Prototyping, Comments, Layers panel). Skipped as not expressible by the chord grammar: mouse-drag actions (marquee-select, duplicate-by-Alt/Option-drag, deep-select by Cmd/Ctrl+click), the 'hold Alt/Option while hovering a field' numeric-scrub modifier, and typing `@` to mention a collaborator in a comment. Also skipped: 'Combine as variants' and redo, since no shortcut for either is documented in the current official Help Center. Version-specific to the current (2026) Figma Design desktop app; some articles describe FigJam or shared UI chrome but the shortcuts quoted from them apply identically in Figma Design.",
